            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:evidence_uuid_gate"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "packages/cli/src/index.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 343,
                  "startLine": 343
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "The hook publishes whatever thread/conversation identifier its runtime environment contains (any string up to 1 KiB), but the watcher requires a UUID-variant shape: an ambient codex/letta runtime whose native id is not a UUID makes watch --deliver exit with a usage error, and at delivery time targetDeliveryKey silently classifies such ids as 'no supported local route'. The publication and consumption sides enforce different identifier formats, so the same value is accepted into presence and then either blocks the watcher from starting or never wakes, leaving a session that presence says is wakeable but that no watcher will ever deliver to."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "2ec3056ac804a36a:1",
            "security/v1": "security/v1:sha256:6f890ce1e63a092752905ee9ef1272605a3d6ba124299a33b085798eb78300a3"
          },
          "properties": {
            "candidateId": "cand-3-runtime-id-uuid-gate",
            "category": "input-validation",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_42a6b1c32db4bb02c30216a5",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_f69fcf61f66a798f256c9fb3",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "validation.inconsistent-identifier-format",
          "ruleIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
