              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "packages/hooks/src/board-hook.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 84,
                  "startLine": 77
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "swallow"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "packages/hooks/src/board-hook.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 93,
                  "startLine": 90
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "During heartbeat and poll, the Claude session-registry write is sequenced before the poll's unread-injection step inside the hook's single error-swallowing try block. When the ~/.board/sessions/claude directory exists with an unexpected owner, mode, or as a symlink, the registry write throws on every invocation and the unread-injection step never runs, while the idle heartbeat still publishes presence including the socket. The session therefore advertises an idle, wakeable-looking presence but silently never receives injected mentions, with nothing reported and no recovery path until the directory is repaired manually."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "478363cb651519fc:1",
            "security/v1": "security/v1:sha256:f50a3e1d7d104df757d22a7929520d7bb022c41c22ab27dd0898c4c7dbeaabab"
          },
